# Validate changed backend APIs locally

When you **add or change** a Nest HTTP route (or the request/response behavior of one), do not finish until that route succeeds against a locally served backend. Unit tests do not replace this call.

## 1. Serve

If `nx serve backend --configuration=development` is not already listening, start it and wait until Nest logs that it is listening. Base URL: `http://localhost:3000/api`. Fix boot failures before calling the API.

## 2. Sign in

Send the OTP to the phone on the account, then confirm with `0000`. Header `x-client-platform: mobile` so the JSON body includes `access_token`.

```http
POST /auth/login/start-otp
{ "email": "besongsamueloru+mm@gmail.com", "channel": "sms" }

POST /auth/login/verify-otp
{ "email": "besongsamueloru+mm@gmail.com", "channel": "sms", "otp": "0000" }
```

Later calls: `Authorization: Bearer <token>` and, when the route is persona-scoped, `X-Active-Persona: client|business|agent`. Do not print or commit the token. If verify fails, stop.

## 3. Call the changed API

Exercise the new or updated route with a real request and the persona it requires. Assert the status and the fields the change is supposed to return or persist. If the call fails, fix the API and call it again.

## 4. Order state

When the route needs an order in a given status, place one on this local server and move it there before the call. Use quantity 1 and keep any Mobile Money charge under 2000 XAF. Drive client, business, and agent with `X-Active-Persona` the same way as `.cursor/skills/run-order-flows/reference.md` (confirm, ready, claim, delivery, or pickup), against `localhost` rather than the dev host. Do not cancel the order unless the route under test is cancel.

## 5. Report

Say the local URL, the route, the HTTP status, and the order id and status when an order was required.
